<!--
  MCU reassembly buffer-pool config — the SSOT for the lwIP (MCU /
  bare-metal) host's reassembly slot-pool dimensions and runtime knobs
  (reassembly-fsm prose-sketch §4 "Timer / quota / pool config").

  R311in — the MCU sibling of `reassembly_pool_ap.scxml`. Same SSOT
  rationale: SCE codegen emits the spec-anchored SLOT_COUNT / SLOT_SIZE /
  MAX_FRAGMENTS_PER_MESSAGE / REASSEMBLY_TIMEOUT_MS / PER_PEER_QUOTA
  constants that the MCU host's `ReassemblyDispatcher` consumes via the
  no-alloc `wz-runtime-coop::reassembly_rx` seam (carry [3]). Both
  profiles source their pool from one SCE-owned scxml each, selecting
  their own machine — the kconfig composable-framework structure.

  Values mirror `deploy/ap_mcu_pair.yaml` `mcu_node.buffer_pools.
  reassembly_pool` (the MCU machine of the canonical asymmetric deploy:
  the smaller, SRAM-resident pool). SCE deploy invariants hold against
  the MCU link mtu 1472 / peer_table 16: slot_size 4096 >= 2*1472 = 2944,
  and peer_table 16 * per_peer_quota 2 = 32 >= slot_count 4.

  MCU footprint (R311in, vendor/sce 4ec1aa642 + fragment.chunk payload
  field removed): the no_std ReassemblyDispatcher<4, 4096> is ~22 KiB,
  resident in the 128 KiB sram2 region. (Before both fixes it was 1.68
  MiB — the per-slot Engine carried a 1472-byte event payload x 64-deep
  queue x 4 slots plus inline W3C event metadata; see the SCE
  no_std-footprint report.)

  cache-policy is `none` here (NOT the deploy.yaml mcu_node's `maintain`):
  the wz reassembly dispatcher stages into its own `BoundedVec`, not the
  §5.E DMA slot table, so it performs no DMA cache maintenance. Emitting
  `maintain` would pull the C5 `sce_dcache_clean_by_addr` /
  `sce_dcache_invalidate_by_addr` externs into the (wz-unused) DMA pool
  API for no benefit. The eventual DMA-staged reassembly path is a
  separate, not-yet-wired concern; the five reassembly constants this
  emit feeds the dispatcher are identical under either cache policy.
-->
<scxml xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml"
       xmlns:sce="http://sce.dev/ext"
       sce:kind="buffer-pool" name="reassembly_pool_mcu" version="1.0">
  <sce:variant>reassembly</sce:variant>
  <sce:slot-count>4</sce:slot-count>
  <sce:slot-size>4096</sce:slot-size>
  <sce:section>sram2</sce:section>
  <sce:alignment>32</sce:alignment>
  <sce:cache-policy>none</sce:cache-policy>
  <sce:max-fragments-per-message>2</sce:max-fragments-per-message>
  <sce:reassembly-timeout-ms>500</sce:reassembly-timeout-ms>
  <sce:per-peer-quota>2</sce:per-peer-quota>
</scxml>
